{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>וַיַּעֲשׂוּ כֵן מֹשֶׁה וְאַהֲרֹן כַּאֲשֶׁר וגו׳</b>. Meaning: when Moses and Aaron performed the act of striking the Nile, the effect was accomplished and the will was fulfilled as though it were a command of HaShem from His mouth, blessed be He, to the Nile that it should turn to blood. And see what I further explained in the verse (Exodus 7:6) ״וַיַּעַשׂ מֹשֶׁה״ etc., the one preceding this, and see in the verse after this one." "<b>לְעֵינֵי פַרְעֹה וּלְעֵינֵי עֲבָדָיו</b>. Although the beginning of His words was with Pharaoh in private, at the time of his withdrawal to attend to his needs, according to their words, their memory for a blessing (Shemot Rabbah 9), and presumably he would be there alone — even so, Scripture informs you that He delayed the striking until he struck publicly, לְעֵינֵי עֲבָדָיו. And although in the command of HaShem this detail was not specified, presumably HaShem did speak it to him accordingly. Or perhaps it is to this that Scripture intends by saying <b>כֵּן כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּה</b> — meaning, just as the things stated in the words of HaShem; and regarding details that you see in their actions that are not written thus in the word of Elohim, Scripture testifies about them that they are כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּה HaShem, and this is correct."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:40.563573903Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}